# centralize_events_chat_alliance_3client_udp — client 1 (slot 0).
# Same shape as the unicast scenario but with an alliance handshake
# in front: c3 requests an alliance with slot 0 (c1), c1 accepts,
# then both exchange unicast chats. The request comes from c3
# because c3 joins last (around c1's tick 112), and the server only
# records a request to a seat that is connected and takes no accept
# without one. The chat path itself is unicast-only on the wire (no
# allies-only destination), so the alliance ceremony is what bakes
# the request/accept event variants into the baseline. c2 (passive
# witness) should see the alliance broadcast events but zero
# CTRL_CHAT events.
{"tick": 250, "op": "alliance_accept", "from": 0, "to": 2}
{"tick": 350, "op": "chat", "dest": 2, "body": "hi ally c3 from c1"}
